---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **언제 가장 넓게 퍼지나.** (`/time-to-peak`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   들어온 자리(/opening)·나가는 자리(/exit)·버틴 주(/run-length)를 쟀는데
 *   **몇 주째에 가장 많은 나라에 동시에 올라 있나**는 안 쟀다. 그것이 「밀어 줄 때」다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **날것의 격차로 안 판다.** 한국 시리즈는 더 오래 가고, 오래 가면 늦게 정점을 찍는 것이 당연하다.
 *    그래서 **길이를 묶은 표를 나란히** 둔다 — 그러면 가운데 띠에서 격차가 거의 사라진다.
 *    ⭐ 그 사실을 감추지 않는다. 그것이 이 지면의 요점이다.
 * ⛔ **얇은 칸을 지운 척하지 않는다.** 1–2주 띠는 한국 시리즈 여섯 편뿐이다 — 적고, 읽지 말라고 적는다.
 * ⛔ 작품을 줄세우지 않는다. 이름을 안 낸다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 * ⚠ 수를 손으로 적지 않는다. 전부 `wikitip-time-to-peak.json` 에서 읽는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-time-to-peak.json';

const 찾 = (g) => d.byGroup.find((x) => x.group === g);
const 한시 = 찾('한국 시리즈'); const 밖시 = 찾('그 밖 시리즈');
const 영어이름 = {
  '한국 시리즈': 'Korean series',
  '그 밖 시리즈': 'Every other series',
  '한국 영화': 'Korean films',
  '그 밖 영화': 'Every other film',
};
const 띠영어 = {
  '1–2주': '1–2 weeks', '3–4주': '3–4 weeks', '5–8주': '5–8 weeks', '9주 이상': '9 weeks or more',
};
const 차례 = ['한국 시리즈', '그 밖 시리즈', '한국 영화', '그 밖 영화'].map(찾);
const 뺀얇은것 = d.byGroup.reduce((s, g) => s + g.droppedThin, 0);
const 뺀열린것 = d.byGroup.reduce((s, g) => s + g.droppedOpenEnded, 0);
const 얇은칸 = 한시.byLengthBand.find((x) => x.band === '1–2주');

const TITLE = 'When a Korean title is at its widest — the week the push has already worked';
const DESC =
  `Korean series are at their widest in their first chart week ${한시.peakInWeekOnePc}% of the time, `
  + `against ${밖시.peakInWeekOnePc}% for every other series. Hold run length fixed and most of that gap `
  + `closes — but among titles lasting nine weeks or more it does not.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10', 'https://www.wikidata.org'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/time-to-peak">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Widest in week one — Korean series <b>{한시.peakInWeekOnePc}%</b> ·
    every other series <b>{밖시.peakInWeekOnePc}%</b>.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Four groups, measured the same way</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th></th><th>Titles</th><th>Median peak week</th>
            <th>Widest in week 1</th><th>Widest by week 4</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {차례.map((g) => (
            <tr class={g.group.startsWith('한국') ? 'edge' : undefined}>
              <td class="nm">{영어이름[g.group]}</td>
              <td>{g.titles.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
              <td>{g.medianWeek}</td>
              <td class="tot">{g.peakInWeekOnePc}%</td>
              <td>{g.peakByWeekFourPc}%</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>{d.unit}</b> {d.threshold}</p>
    <p class="note fine">
      {d.whyOpenEndedRemoved} That is {뺀열린것} titles, alongside{' '}
      {뺀얇은것.toLocaleString('en-US')} that reached fewer than {d.countryThreshold} countries.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="warn-box">
    <h2>Most of that gap is length, and here is the proof</h2>
    <p class="warn">
      Korean series <a href="/run-length">last longer than other series</a>. A longer run has more
      later weeks in it, so peaking late is partly just having a late to peak in. The same
      measurement inside bands of equal run length:
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Weeks on a chart</th><th>Korean series</th><th>Every other series</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {한시.byLengthBand.map((a) => {
            const b = 밖시.byLengthBand.find((x) => x.band === a.band);
            return (
              <tr class={a.band === '9주 이상' ? 'edge' : undefined}>
                <td class="nm">{띠영어[a.band]}</td>
                <td class="tot">{a.peakInWeekOnePc}% <span class="fine">({a.titles})</span></td>
                <td>{b.peakInWeekOnePc}% <span class="fine">({b.titles})</span></td>
              </tr>
            );
          })}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      <b>In the middle it nearly disappears.</b> Among titles that lasted five to eight weeks the two
      groups are within a couple of points of each other. Most of the headline gap is that Korean
      series are concentrated in the long bands, where everybody peaks late.
    </p>
    <p class="q">
      <b>But it does not close everywhere.</b> Among titles lasting nine weeks or more, Korean series
      peak in week one{' '}
      <b>{한시.byLengthBand.find((x) => x.band === '9주 이상').peakInWeekOnePc}%</b> of the time
      against <b>{밖시.byLengthBand.find((x) => x.band === '9주 이상').peakInWeekOnePc}%</b>.
    </p>
    <p class="note fine">
      ⚠ The top band is {얇은칸.titles} Korean titles. It is printed because leaving a row out of a
      table is its own kind of claim, but nothing should be read from it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this is worth knowing for</h2>
    <p class="body">
      <b>{한시.peakByWeekFourPc}% of Korean series have reached their widest point by week four.</b>{' '}
      That is the window. Inside it the median is <b>week {한시.medianWeek}</b>, not week one — so a
      push timed to the first Monday is timed to a week that, four times in five, is not the widest.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      After week four there is very little left: the remainder is spread from week five to week{' '}
      {한시.latestWeek}.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted, and what it cannot say</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Rows read</b> — {d.rowsRead.toLocaleString('en-US')}.</li>
      <li><b>Why every other title too</b> — {d.whyOthersToo}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="warn">{d.cannotAnswer}</p>
    <p class="note">
      This is a distribution, not a rule. Some Korean series are widest in week one and some in week{' '}
      {한시.latestWeek}. The table says how often, not what will happen to any one title.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/opening">What an opening position buys</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/run-length">How long a title holds a chart</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/arrival">Does it arrive in one country or many</a> · <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/time-to-peak" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn-box { border-left: 3px solid #b45309; padding-left: 1rem; }
</style>
